1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
The example interior is 14 cells wide and 3 high: 42 cells, excluding boundary tiles.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Each cot occupies 2 x 2 cells. The example height of 3 is not a fixed barracks requirement.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A duplicant picks up sandstone for the example cots.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Carry material to the blueprint. Delivery requires a reachable route.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Deliver the material and prepare to construct.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The duplicant constructs the cot. The completed blueprint becomes a cot.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Repeat for the remaining cots. Repeated construction is condensed here.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Enclose the barracks with tiles, leaving a doorway. Tile construction is condensed here.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
A vertical manual airlock occupies 1 x 2 cells. Fill the tiles above it to enclose the room.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Check the room overlay: 12-64 interior cells, at least one bed, and no industrial machinery.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The 42-cell example fits the size limit. Check cot access, assignments and sleep schedules; tasks use your colony.
